WEBVTT

00:39.039 --> 00:41.583
"You are a carcinogen,"

00:41.584 --> 00:43.085
I would say to her.

00:44.712 --> 00:46.337
"You are a tumor,

00:46.338 --> 00:48.298
"whose malignancy has defined

00:48.299 --> 00:51.217
"the ebb and flow
of all I've done,

00:51.218 --> 00:53.303
"of all I've tried to do.

00:53.304 --> 00:54.429
"And yet, in spite of that,

00:54.430 --> 00:56.556
"do you know how much space
you occupy

00:56.557 --> 00:58.559
"in the entirety of me?

00:59.435 --> 01:00.686
"This much.

01:01.687 --> 01:02.896
"You define my life,

01:02.897 --> 01:06.816
"and yet, this is how much
you matter to me.

01:06.817 --> 01:08.985
"If you hadn't shown up
on my door this morning,

01:08.986 --> 01:11.237
"I'd have gladly gone
the rest of my days

01:11.238 --> 01:12.697
"thinking of you regularly,

01:12.698 --> 01:14.365
"but from a distance,

01:14.366 --> 01:15.993
"flung from your orbit.

01:16.744 --> 01:17.912
"But now...

01:18.829 --> 01:20.914
"you are here

01:20.915 --> 01:25.376
"and the bile is rising
and taking the form of words.

01:25.377 --> 01:27.504
"And what these words mean is,

01:27.505 --> 01:28.755
"never have I known

01:28.756 --> 01:30.924
"how closely love
and hate are bound

01:30.925 --> 01:33.092
"than when I think of you
and realize

01:33.093 --> 01:34.762
"you deserve neither."

01:59.995 --> 02:04.374
♪ I'll kill you softly ♪

02:04.375 --> 02:08.170
♪ So sweetly, kindly ♪

02:09.004 --> 02:13.466
♪ I'm mesmerizing ♪

02:13.467 --> 02:17.095
♪ It's terrifying ♪

02:29.024 --> 02:30.733
♪ This black suit fits
like a glove ♪

02:30.734 --> 02:33.570
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

02:33.571 --> 02:35.321
♪ Won't lose myself
to a touch ♪

02:35.322 --> 02:36.949
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

02:38.033 --> 02:39.701
♪ This black suit fits
like a glove ♪

02:39.702 --> 02:42.453
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

02:42.454 --> 02:43.830
♪ My red heart freed
like a dove ♪

02:43.831 --> 02:45.540
♪ But you tell me
that it's never enough ♪

02:45.541 --> 02:46.666
♪ This is your burial ♪

02:54.800 --> 02:56.176
♪ This is your burial ♪

03:03.559 --> 03:04.934
♪ This is your burial ♪

03:41.013 --> 03:42.555
♪ This black suit fits
like a glove ♪

03:42.556 --> 03:45.183
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

03:45.184 --> 03:46.976
♪ Won't lose myself
to a touch ♪

03:46.977 --> 03:49.854
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

03:49.855 --> 03:51.606
♪ This black suit
fits like a glove ♪

03:51.607 --> 03:53.232
♪ But your teeth
tell me I'm not enough ♪

03:53.233 --> 03:54.693
♪ This is your burial ♪

04:10.417 --> 04:12.460
I hadn't seen her
in over 10 years.

04:12.461 --> 04:15.506
But I could tell she was
coming from a mile away.

04:17.091 --> 04:18.592
More than a mile.

04:19.218 --> 04:21.970
A thousand miles.

04:21.971 --> 04:24.806
I woke up that morning
with a taste in my mouth

04:24.807 --> 04:27.309
I hadn't felt in years.

04:34.441 --> 04:36.859
Is it... Is it a bit too rigid
here at the waist?

04:36.860 --> 04:38.362
How do you feel?
You feel okay?

04:39.196 --> 04:40.488
Yeah. I just... It's...

04:40.489 --> 04:42.658
- I do love how bold it is.
- Yeah.

04:43.617 --> 04:44.702
A whole new you.

04:46.537 --> 04:48.163
I cast it
out of my mind,

04:48.872 --> 04:50.457
but as the day went on,

04:51.375 --> 04:53.251
the taste left my mouth

04:53.252 --> 04:56.713
and traveled
to that space behind my eyes

04:56.714 --> 04:59.799
where it settled
and turned thick.

04:59.800 --> 05:02.593
By the time the late flights
from LAX to Heathrow

05:02.594 --> 05:04.053
were coming in
for their landing,

05:04.054 --> 05:07.933
I felt as if a secret twin
had grown in my skull.

05:21.155 --> 05:22.948
What's wrong?
Are you okay?

06:05.157 --> 06:06.408
It was calling,

06:07.576 --> 06:08.827
shouting,

06:11.872 --> 06:12.915
screaming,

06:15.626 --> 06:16.752
telling me

06:17.461 --> 06:18.754
it was coming.

06:20.214 --> 06:22.257
She was coming.

06:24.218 --> 06:25.511
She was here.

07:12.224 --> 07:14.475
Uh, hi. Excuse me.
Hi. Can I help you?

07:14.476 --> 07:15.852
I'm looking for Sam.

07:15.853 --> 07:19.730
Oh, I'm afraid
Sam isn't available right now.

07:19.731 --> 07:20.940
Are you...

07:20.941 --> 07:22.108
Does Sam know you were coming?

07:22.109 --> 07:23.192
No, no.

07:23.193 --> 07:24.443
Okay, uh...

07:24.444 --> 07:27.114
Well, then could I just
ask you to just wait, uh...

07:28.157 --> 07:29.199
Sam?

07:29.700 --> 07:31.784
Sam?

07:31.785 --> 07:33.035
Um...

07:33.036 --> 07:35.329
- Sam?
- Sorry, you really can't...

07:35.330 --> 07:37.373
Uh...
Sam?

07:37.374 --> 07:38.833
Sam's not
seeing anybody

07:38.834 --> 07:40.043
- right now.
- Sam?

07:44.923 --> 07:46.174
Sam, I'm so sorry.

07:46.175 --> 07:48.594
I didn't see her coming,
she just came in.

07:51.054 --> 07:52.472
Sam, I need a dress.

07:56.518 --> 07:58.603
Just landed?

07:58.604 --> 07:59.938
Yes.
From LA?

08:00.731 --> 08:02.356
Yes, I just came from...

08:02.357 --> 08:03.817
Would you like
something to eat?

08:04.568 --> 08:07.320
- Uh... No, I...
- Hilda,

08:07.321 --> 08:10.656
do we... do we have anything
to eat here?

08:10.657 --> 08:12.700
Um, not really, no.

08:12.701 --> 08:14.494
Okay.
Well, there you go.

08:16.371 --> 08:17.915
Does anyone know you're here?

08:19.625 --> 08:21.417
- No.
-I... I...

08:21.418 --> 08:24.003
I must say,
I wish you had called.

08:24.004 --> 08:26.088
You might have noticed
we're a little underwater

08:26.089 --> 08:27.965
- at the moment.
- Would you have answered?

08:27.966 --> 08:29.842
No,
but somebody would have.

08:29.843 --> 08:32.845
And they could have told you
we're very busy.

08:32.846 --> 08:34.556
Sam has her show coming up.

08:35.265 --> 08:36.642
Oh.

08:37.267 --> 08:38.267
Sorry.

08:38.268 --> 08:41.063
For not calling
or for just showing up?

08:42.064 --> 08:43.648
In general.

08:43.649 --> 08:47.193
Wouldn't you rather get
more specific?

08:47.194 --> 08:50.404
I just never had the chance
to say it before,

08:50.405 --> 08:53.491
- so...
- So the onus is on me then,

08:53.492 --> 08:55.826
to list off your offenses
one by one

08:55.827 --> 08:56.869
and cross-check them

08:56.870 --> 09:00.207
against the totality
of your "I'm sorry"?

09:01.250 --> 09:02.708
Oh, well.

09:02.709 --> 09:05.712
That hardly seems worth it,
does it?

09:06.588 --> 09:08.089
Making me do all the work,

09:08.090 --> 09:10.341
- just like you always do.
- I can go

09:10.342 --> 09:11.384
if you want.

09:11.385 --> 09:14.553
If you want to go, go.

09:14.554 --> 09:16.055
If you want to stay, stay.

09:16.056 --> 09:18.224
If you want to apologize,
you go for it.

09:18.225 --> 09:19.725
But if you stay,

09:19.726 --> 09:20.977
please stop doing

09:20.978 --> 09:22.228
that hovering thing
you always do,

09:22.229 --> 09:24.064
because it makes me
very nervous.

09:25.357 --> 09:28.110
- Sorry.
- You already said that.

09:29.611 --> 09:31.320
- I mean it.
- Say it two more times,

09:31.321 --> 09:32.614
so I believe you.

09:34.783 --> 09:36.201
But not yet.

09:37.494 --> 09:41.290
Catch me by surprise
with your sincerity.

09:42.666 --> 09:46.086
Now, why don't you start
with why you're here?

09:46.795 --> 09:48.004
I really do need a dress.

09:48.005 --> 09:50.548
What, you don't have
a whole coterie of stylists

09:50.549 --> 09:52.300
to take care of that for you?

09:52.301 --> 09:54.636
No, I do. But it's not...

09:57.014 --> 09:58.097
working out.

09:58.098 --> 10:00.308
And this performance,
when is it?

10:00.309 --> 10:01.685
The 31st.

10:02.602 --> 10:04.730
- That's on Sunday?
- Yes.

10:05.480 --> 10:07.566
And today is?

10:09.484 --> 10:10.569
Thursday.

10:12.029 --> 10:14.613
Well, that's impossible.

10:14.614 --> 10:16.490
What's wrong
with the dress you have?

10:16.491 --> 10:18.117
I'm assuming you have one.

10:18.118 --> 10:19.745
It's just all wrong.

10:20.370 --> 10:21.747
May I see it?

10:24.207 --> 10:26.501
- So that's it?
-Yes.

10:27.377 --> 10:28.754
It's not a dress at all.

10:29.421 --> 10:30.921
Who made it?

10:30.922 --> 10:32.299
Saracen & Pare.

10:34.760 --> 10:36.719
Hmm.

10:36.720 --> 10:39.473
Tell me three things
that are wrong with it.

10:40.474 --> 10:42.017
It doesn't feel like me.

10:43.226 --> 10:46.021
Okay. It doesn't
feel like you. That's one.

10:47.481 --> 10:48.523
That's it.

10:49.232 --> 10:50.484
That's it?

10:51.360 --> 10:53.527
- Yes.
- So you,

10:53.528 --> 10:57.406
who have been dressed
by everyone

10:57.407 --> 10:59.283
and worn everything,

10:59.284 --> 11:01.786
who once paraded down
a red...  ...carpet

11:01.787 --> 11:04.246
wearing nothing
but freshly poured honey,

11:04.247 --> 11:06.665
you have somehow found

11:06.666 --> 11:09.001
the one outfit
in all of creation

11:09.002 --> 11:11.629
that doesn't feel like you?

11:11.630 --> 11:12.546
Yes.

11:12.547 --> 11:15.132
And you've come
crawling back to me

11:15.133 --> 11:17.968
because you know
I can do better?

11:17.969 --> 11:20.221
- Yes.
- Because I, above all others,

11:20.222 --> 11:21.680
know you?

11:21.681 --> 11:23.225
Because I didn't know
where else to go.

11:23.934 --> 11:24.976
Truly?

11:26.019 --> 11:27.229
Yes.

11:33.860 --> 11:36.780
Will you let me do
whatever I like?

11:38.031 --> 11:39.490
Yes. But...

11:39.491 --> 11:41.284
Will you do exactly as I say?

11:41.827 --> 11:43.327
Yes, within...

11:43.328 --> 11:45.205
And will you wear what I make?

11:46.248 --> 11:47.457
Yes.

11:48.083 --> 11:49.501
And can you stop time?

11:53.922 --> 11:55.172
Just did.

11:57.342 --> 11:59.927
This is really
going to take some doing,

11:59.928 --> 12:02.221
if we're gonna pull this off.

12:02.222 --> 12:04.473
Just tell me
what I can do.

12:04.474 --> 12:06.225
You can just
keep talking.

12:06.226 --> 12:07.351
That's how this works.

12:07.352 --> 12:10.312
You tell me something
like how you're feeling,

12:10.313 --> 12:13.858
and I'll take those feelings
and turn them into a dress.

12:13.859 --> 12:17.945
The transubstantiation
of feeling.

12:17.946 --> 12:19.364
That's what we're doing here.

12:21.992 --> 12:23.325
Here we are.

12:23.326 --> 12:25.286
Now, as you can see,

12:25.287 --> 12:27.913
I've entered
my Ms. Havisham period

12:27.914 --> 12:29.832
very much ahead of schedule.

12:29.833 --> 12:33.086
This is where I come to cry
my eyes out in the dark.

12:40.719 --> 12:41.845
Stand here, please.

12:50.520 --> 12:52.730
Now, uh...

12:52.731 --> 12:56.358
I haven't had a new idea
in ages.

12:56.359 --> 12:57.902
Not a good one, at least.

12:57.903 --> 12:59.487
So if we're to do this,

12:59.488 --> 13:02.281
I'm just gonna
have to fasten things to you

13:02.282 --> 13:05.285
until inspiration strikes.

13:07.579 --> 13:08.663
There we go.

13:13.585 --> 13:16.129
Uh, can I take
your sweater?

13:17.756 --> 13:18.756
Yes.

13:18.757 --> 13:19.883
- Thank you.
- Mmm-hmm.

13:21.134 --> 13:22.135
So...

13:23.512 --> 13:26.889
So tell me more
about this dress we're making.

13:26.890 --> 13:28.934
What do you see in your head?

13:30.560 --> 13:31.603
Just...

13:33.146 --> 13:34.271
me.

13:34.272 --> 13:35.315
Just you?

13:35.982 --> 13:37.067
But...

13:38.401 --> 13:40.110
But all of me.

13:40.111 --> 13:44.031
I was thinking more like,
"What color?"

13:44.032 --> 13:45.367
- Uh...
- Hold still.

13:48.662 --> 13:49.996
Whatever you like.

13:50.455 --> 13:51.622
But no red.

13:51.623 --> 13:53.083
Do you have to be able
to move?

13:54.042 --> 13:55.417
- Yes.
- Dance?

13:55.418 --> 13:58.170
- Yes.
- Any stunts or harnesses?

13:58.171 --> 13:59.213
No.

13:59.214 --> 14:00.297
Backup dancers?

14:00.298 --> 14:01.590
- Nine.
- I'm not making

14:01.591 --> 14:02.883
- anything for them.
- I know.

14:02.884 --> 14:03.968
There's simply
not enough time.

14:03.969 --> 14:05.762
I know. You don't have to.
Just me.

14:06.263 --> 14:07.305
Arms up.

14:11.268 --> 14:12.644
What song are you singing?

14:15.105 --> 14:16.689
Spooky Action.

14:16.690 --> 14:18.275
Hmm. I don't remember
that one.

14:19.025 --> 14:21.068
- 'Cause it's new.
- Oh.

14:21.069 --> 14:22.653
That explains it then.

14:22.654 --> 14:23.905
Did you write it?

14:24.698 --> 14:26.032
Yes.

14:28.535 --> 14:30.160
I'll play it for you
if you want.

14:30.161 --> 14:31.496
Yes, maybe later.

14:34.541 --> 14:35.666
It's good.

14:35.667 --> 14:37.836
I am sure it is.

14:38.837 --> 14:40.045
It might be
the best song ever written

14:40.046 --> 14:42.006
- in the history of songs.
-Mmm.

14:42.007 --> 14:43.633
Lift your shirt up
for me, please.

14:55.353 --> 14:56.646
You've gotten so tiny.

14:57.397 --> 14:58.982
The tiniest intruder.

15:01.901 --> 15:03.485
You're exactly the same.

15:03.486 --> 15:04.654
Oh, no, I'm not.

15:05.405 --> 15:06.489
You'll see.

15:07.490 --> 15:09.576
You'll see how I've changed.

15:11.036 --> 15:13.121
What the years
have made of me.

15:16.916 --> 15:19.169
Okay. That's good for now.
Thank you, Hilda.

15:26.635 --> 15:28.385
- Hilda.
- Yes?

15:28.386 --> 15:31.055
Hilda, would you run back
to the main house

15:31.056 --> 15:34.017
- and grab a few things for me?
- Mmm-hmm.

15:35.435 --> 15:37.062
What does this matter?

15:38.229 --> 15:40.147
- You know what I need?
- Of course.

15:40.148 --> 15:41.899
Uh, what about you?
Can we get you anything?

15:41.900 --> 15:44.109
- I'm fine. Thank you.
-Okay. Good.

15:44.110 --> 15:45.654
Okay.
I'll be right back.

16:04.881 --> 16:06.173
She's not gonna tell anyone...

16:06.174 --> 16:08.050
No. Don't worry.

16:08.051 --> 16:09.843
There are no spies
in our midst.

16:09.844 --> 16:14.348
I just need her
to bring me some things.

16:14.349 --> 16:17.059
Some old bric-a-brac,
a few bolts of fabric,

16:17.060 --> 16:18.435
and a good pair of scissors

16:18.436 --> 16:20.729
in case one of us has
the sudden desire to...

16:28.738 --> 16:30.572
Okay.

17:05.191 --> 17:06.526
How's your mum?

17:08.862 --> 17:10.029
She died.

17:12.198 --> 17:13.199
I'm sorry.

17:15.702 --> 17:17.871
How are you?

17:22.000 --> 17:23.125
Same.

17:23.126 --> 17:25.419
You've been laying low.

17:25.420 --> 17:28.922
Am I right that this will be
your first outing

17:28.923 --> 17:30.799
- since...
- Since?

17:30.800 --> 17:33.969
Since whatever happened
happened.

17:33.970 --> 17:35.763
What do you think happened?

17:35.764 --> 17:38.307
Well, I... I saw that video.

17:38.308 --> 17:40.268
Everyone saw that video.

17:41.311 --> 17:42.812
Is there more to it than that?

17:45.482 --> 17:46.524
Yes.

17:48.610 --> 17:51.487
And when it first happened,
people kept asking me,

17:51.488 --> 17:52.821
what do I know,

17:52.822 --> 17:55.492
had I heard anything,
"Did she trip, did she jump?"

17:58.495 --> 17:59.703
What'd you say?

17:59.704 --> 18:02.122
People... said
you had a breakdown.

18:02.123 --> 18:04.625
I said, "No. She probably
just needed a break."

18:04.626 --> 18:07.253
Yeah. That was part of it.

18:09.339 --> 18:10.924
What are the other parts?

18:13.635 --> 18:14.928
I don't want to tell you.

18:15.553 --> 18:17.180
Why?

18:17.931 --> 18:19.598
Because you'd laugh.

18:19.599 --> 18:21.391
- No, I wouldn't.
- Yes, you would.

18:21.392 --> 18:23.101
You're laughing right now.

18:23.102 --> 18:24.394
I'm just...

18:24.395 --> 18:26.271
I'm just picturing
the worst possible thing

18:26.272 --> 18:28.107
that could have made you do
what you did.

18:28.650 --> 18:30.068
I...

18:31.194 --> 18:33.487
- What is it?
- It's not worth mentioning,

18:33.488 --> 18:35.864
but it's very funny.

18:35.865 --> 18:37.866
Well, that's why
I'm not gonna tell you.

18:37.867 --> 18:39.034
Except you will.

18:39.035 --> 18:41.161
Because you never would have

18:41.162 --> 18:42.621
brought it up
in the first place

18:42.622 --> 18:44.206
if you didn't want to.

18:44.207 --> 18:46.416
No, you want to tell me.

18:46.417 --> 18:48.919
You want me to know so badly,
you can hardly stand it.

18:48.920 --> 18:51.506
But it's okay. I can wait.

18:56.886 --> 18:59.013
Mmm. Mmm.

19:03.768 --> 19:04.978
No.

19:08.273 --> 19:09.566
No.

19:13.361 --> 19:14.404
Mmm.

19:45.226 --> 19:46.477
No.

19:51.065 --> 19:53.192
Right. No red.

19:55.486 --> 19:57.029
No red.

19:57.030 --> 19:59.907
What about your hair,
what's going on there?

19:59.908 --> 20:01.158
We should...

20:01.159 --> 20:02.576
We should talk
about your halo.

20:02.577 --> 20:03.578
No halo.

20:04.704 --> 20:05.996
At all?

20:05.997 --> 20:08.749
I want to get back
to the basics.

20:08.750 --> 20:11.293
I mean, it doesn't get
much more basic than that.

20:11.294 --> 20:12.836
It's sort of your thing.

20:12.837 --> 20:14.463
It was never meant
to be my thing.

20:14.464 --> 20:15.797
It was your thing.

20:15.798 --> 20:18.383
That's... that's not
how I recall it.

20:18.384 --> 20:19.384
But whatever the case,

20:19.385 --> 20:20.719
you've done
pretty well with it.

20:20.720 --> 20:22.971
- We'll do well without it.
- Will anyone recognize you

20:22.972 --> 20:24.139
without it?

20:24.140 --> 20:26.683
I don't know if anyone
actually truly comprehends

20:26.684 --> 20:28.561
- the shape of your...
- They hurt.

20:34.442 --> 20:37.319
Well, that's because whoever's
making them for you now

20:37.320 --> 20:38.947
keeps trying to up the ante.

20:40.031 --> 20:41.907
They're not doing it right.

20:41.908 --> 20:42.991
I could make you a new one

20:42.992 --> 20:44.368
- in two seconds flat...
- No.

20:44.369 --> 20:46.495
- Right. But, don't you...
- I said...

20:46.496 --> 20:48.121
Yes, I know what you said.

20:48.122 --> 20:49.373
You don't want to wear one,

20:49.374 --> 20:51.918
but what if I want you
to wear one?

20:55.546 --> 20:58.091
♪ I can't believe
what I found ♪

20:59.926 --> 21:04.513
♪ I'm staring into the dark
so powerful... ♪

21:04.514 --> 21:07.141
♪ My knees are pressed
to the ground ♪

21:08.893 --> 21:11.728
♪ I'm holdin' on
for dear life ♪

21:11.729 --> 21:13.689
♪ It's mythical ♪

21:13.690 --> 21:15.899
♪ Are you there?
Are you mine? ♪

21:15.900 --> 21:17.985
♪ Do you feel holy? ♪

21:17.986 --> 21:20.320
♪ Are you real or divine? ♪

21:20.321 --> 21:22.489
♪ Do you feel holy? ♪

21:22.490 --> 21:24.783
♪ Are you there?
Are you mine? ♪

21:24.784 --> 21:26.118
♪ Do you know? ♪

21:26.119 --> 21:30.080
♪ Your spirit is calling me ♪

21:30.081 --> 21:31.791
What are we doing here?

21:32.875 --> 21:35.128
Are we reinventing you?

21:37.880 --> 21:38.923
No.

21:41.050 --> 21:42.468
No, I...

21:44.554 --> 21:45.555
Just...

21:48.933 --> 21:51.019
I... I want to be...

21:52.353 --> 21:56.024
- Revelatory.
- No. I just, like... I want...

21:57.400 --> 21:59.317
Profundity.

21:59.318 --> 22:01.154
Mmm, more, um...

22:03.823 --> 22:06.783
- Authenticity.
- No. It's like...

22:12.081 --> 22:13.374
Clarity.

22:15.209 --> 22:16.668
- Yes.
- Clarity.

22:16.669 --> 22:19.880
- So, reducing?
- Yes.

22:19.881 --> 22:22.507
- Peeling away everything...
- Yes. Yes.

22:22.508 --> 22:24.634
- ...that's accumulated.
- Yes.

22:24.635 --> 22:26.053
- Old skin.
- Yes.

22:26.054 --> 22:27.512
- Barnacles.
- Yes

22:27.513 --> 22:28.722
Dead hair.

22:28.723 --> 22:30.182
Yes.

22:30.183 --> 22:31.768
All the old yous.

22:32.477 --> 22:33.977
I want to be sharp.

22:33.978 --> 22:36.188
You want me
to make you into a knife?

22:36.189 --> 22:37.774
I want to have a point.

22:39.442 --> 22:40.610
Got it.

22:42.987 --> 22:44.321
If this were
the first performance

22:44.322 --> 22:46.698
I ever gave,
how would you dress me?

22:46.699 --> 22:49.242
I did dress you
for your first performance.

22:49.243 --> 22:50.952
If it were
my last performance?

22:50.953 --> 22:52.580
Is that what this is?

22:53.456 --> 22:54.915
- Maybe.
- 'Cause I could make you

22:54.916 --> 22:56.833
a funeral gown,

22:56.834 --> 22:58.251
if that's what
you really wanted.

22:58.252 --> 22:59.377
I could build you a pyre

22:59.378 --> 23:01.088
the likes of which
the world has never seen

23:01.089 --> 23:03.341
if that's the way
you see things going.

23:07.178 --> 23:08.763
I sort of do.

23:11.057 --> 23:12.600
We are still speaking in...

23:13.559 --> 23:14.977
abstractions, aren't we?

23:17.271 --> 23:18.314
I think so.

23:18.815 --> 23:20.398
Are you depressed?

23:20.399 --> 23:22.109
- No. No.
- Is this a cry for help?

23:22.110 --> 23:24.778
So you're not planning
on self-immolating

23:24.779 --> 23:26.279
on my doorstep?

23:26.280 --> 23:27.531
- No.
- Good.

23:27.532 --> 23:29.658
But if I did, it would be
kind of a great way to go.

23:29.659 --> 23:31.827
No, not for me. I'd be the one
to have to clean you up.

23:31.828 --> 23:33.329
No peeking.

23:36.207 --> 23:37.542
If it's really that bad,

23:38.459 --> 23:39.501
just quit.

23:39.502 --> 23:41.086
I can't quit.

23:41.087 --> 23:42.587
Yeah, you can.

23:42.588 --> 23:44.172
People say
quitting is for cowards,

23:44.173 --> 23:45.757
but it's actually
one of the bravest things

23:45.758 --> 23:48.510
- anyone can do.
- No.

23:48.511 --> 23:51.472
I can't quit. I don't know
how to do anything else.

23:56.894 --> 23:58.353
I just wish
I was happy doing it.

23:58.354 --> 24:00.355
Oh, yes, I remember.

24:00.356 --> 24:05.318
Used to be so happy
singing sad songs. Well...

24:05.319 --> 24:08.489
things are never gonna
be like that ever again.

24:09.407 --> 24:12.242
Nevertheless...
you will go on.

24:12.243 --> 24:13.952
This won't be
your last performance ever

24:13.953 --> 24:15.745
but it will be your best.

24:15.746 --> 24:17.539
You will be radiant,

24:17.540 --> 24:19.374
and transcendent.

24:19.375 --> 24:22.419
And when you open your mouth
and sing about your sadness,

24:22.420 --> 24:23.962
it will be everyone's sadness,

24:23.963 --> 24:27.007
and it will be writ
as large as the goddamn sky

24:27.008 --> 24:29.677
because that's
what you give people.

24:30.636 --> 24:32.470
It's what
you can do for people

24:32.471 --> 24:34.723
and since they pay you for it,

24:34.724 --> 24:36.726
it's more or less your job,
so quit...

24:37.393 --> 24:38.686
or do a good job.

24:45.151 --> 24:46.152
See?

24:47.862 --> 24:49.530
This is what you do.

24:50.990 --> 24:53.576
This is why you have
nothing to worry about.

24:54.952 --> 24:58.247
You give people the gift
of giving a shit about you.

24:59.415 --> 25:03.294
I am humbled
by your munificence.

25:07.590 --> 25:08.591
Uh...

25:09.342 --> 25:11.344
Is someone playing before you?

25:12.637 --> 25:14.137
Yes.

25:14.138 --> 25:15.472
Who?

25:15.473 --> 25:17.349
Miel Contrera.

25:17.350 --> 25:18.767
What's she sing?

25:18.768 --> 25:21.479
- Paper Moon.
- Oh, right. Yeah, I like her.

25:22.396 --> 25:24.272
Everyone likes her.

25:24.273 --> 25:25.650
You sound bitter.

25:27.818 --> 25:28.945
No, I don't.

25:29.946 --> 25:31.321
She's my friend.

25:31.322 --> 25:32.989
- Is she?
- Yes.

25:32.990 --> 25:34.157
- We sang together at the...
- Yeah.

25:34.158 --> 25:36.326
But she was just a child then.

25:36.327 --> 25:37.577
Now I see her
everywhere I look.

25:37.578 --> 25:40.580
Her tits are spilling out
over Soho in Givenchy.

25:40.581 --> 25:42.166
She's successful

25:42.750 --> 25:43.917
and I'm proud of her.

25:43.918 --> 25:46.002
And I'm very happy
to be in her company.

25:46.003 --> 25:47.004
Good.

25:47.505 --> 25:49.256
But?

25:49.257 --> 25:52.676
You're going to lay waste
to her, aren't you?

25:52.677 --> 25:54.427
- What?
- Oh.

25:54.428 --> 25:56.888
Poor girl doesn't know
what she's in for.

25:56.889 --> 25:58.265
Why would you even say that?

25:58.266 --> 25:59.474
Because it's true.

25:59.475 --> 26:00.642
No, it's not.

26:00.643 --> 26:02.269
Oh,
it's already happened.

26:02.270 --> 26:04.437
You don't even have to try.

26:04.438 --> 26:05.855
This is what you do.
You're always picking

26:05.856 --> 26:08.024
- and picking and scratching...
- It's part of my job.

26:08.025 --> 26:09.859
I need to see
what I'm meant to cover.

26:09.860 --> 26:11.820
You mean you need to see
what you want to find.

26:11.821 --> 26:13.071
And if you don't find it,
you put it there

26:13.072 --> 26:14.698
because it suits you
and what you want to make,

26:14.699 --> 26:16.409
- which is why...
- Which is why I'm here

26:17.076 --> 26:18.576
- and you're there.
- No.

26:18.577 --> 26:20.078
I'm here because I want
what you want,

26:20.079 --> 26:22.247
but I want you to want it
for the right reasons.

26:22.248 --> 26:23.456
Which are?

26:23.457 --> 26:24.541
I want you
to have an open heart.

26:24.542 --> 26:26.626
-Mmm-hmm. Mmm.
- And no fear.

26:26.627 --> 26:28.586
And what am I afraid of?

26:28.587 --> 26:29.630
Of this.

26:30.089 --> 26:31.381
- Me.
- Yeah.

26:31.382 --> 26:32.842
Hey,
you're fucking terrifying.

26:34.802 --> 26:36.886
This is what you do.

26:36.887 --> 26:38.596
This is what you do when
you don't know what to do.

26:38.597 --> 26:39.848
This is what
you've always done,

26:39.849 --> 26:42.851
which is why I'm trying
to lay it all out for you.

26:42.852 --> 26:44.978
But I asked you
to lay it out for me

26:44.979 --> 26:47.105
so that I'd know what to do.

26:47.106 --> 26:49.358
- So, here it is.
- Thank you.

26:53.112 --> 26:55.323
Miel Contrera
will sing before me.

26:56.699 --> 27:00.286
She will sing Paper Moon,
and it'll be beautiful.

27:00.786 --> 27:02.162
And then,

27:02.163 --> 27:04.749
at five minutes to midnight,
the lights will go down.

27:06.917 --> 27:08.002
And I...

27:10.629 --> 27:11.756
Mmm-hmm.

27:15.134 --> 27:17.970
I'll do whatever it is
that I'm gonna do.

27:20.723 --> 27:23.433
Sing your new song?

27:23.434 --> 27:24.435
Yes.

27:25.770 --> 27:27.479
Maybe not.

27:27.480 --> 27:30.231
- No, I'm gonna sing it.
- Oh, good.

27:30.232 --> 27:33.194
Because you sounded
uncertain there for a moment.

27:34.612 --> 27:36.655
No, it's just...

27:37.323 --> 27:38.574
It's not good enough yet?

27:43.496 --> 27:44.622
You want to hear it?

27:45.498 --> 27:46.873
The... the song?

27:46.874 --> 27:48.793
- Yes.
- No.

27:50.002 --> 27:51.796
No. No music.

27:52.797 --> 27:53.881
Not right now.

27:54.632 --> 27:56.925
- Why?
- Because if I did,

27:56.926 --> 27:58.218
I'd make a dress for the song.

27:58.219 --> 28:00.512
And you want me to make
a dress for you, don't you?

28:00.513 --> 28:03.140
So, better not to hear it.

28:05.351 --> 28:07.018
You might like it.

28:07.019 --> 28:09.480
Mmm, I'm in an ascetic phase
right now.

28:10.189 --> 28:12.149
I'm trying not liking things.

28:15.277 --> 28:17.696
Why is it called
Spooky Action anyway?

28:18.823 --> 28:21.825
Is it about particle physics?

28:21.826 --> 28:23.786
Large Hadron Colliders?

28:25.913 --> 28:28.874
No. It's more like...

28:29.875 --> 28:31.960
connections we can't explain.

28:31.961 --> 28:34.630
And what led you to write it?

28:37.591 --> 28:40.469
I had a connection
and I couldn't explain it.

28:41.053 --> 28:42.096
To a person?

28:43.097 --> 28:44.140
Maybe.

28:44.932 --> 28:46.016
Are you being coy?

28:46.642 --> 28:48.059
No.

28:48.060 --> 28:49.437
And you really can
dance to it?

28:51.230 --> 28:52.690
- Yes.
- Hmm.

28:54.733 --> 28:55.734
Show me.

28:57.319 --> 28:59.029
- The dance?
- Yeah.

28:59.864 --> 29:01.364
Could you?

29:01.365 --> 29:04.617
Honestly, it'll be good for me
to see how you move

29:04.618 --> 29:06.620
to make sure
I'm accommodating.

29:11.083 --> 29:12.292
Okay.

29:12.293 --> 29:14.462
I'm sure you're supposed to be
drilling it anyway.

29:38.277 --> 29:40.738
Do you have a speaker
or anything I can plug into?

29:41.322 --> 29:42.906
Yeah.

29:42.907 --> 29:44.158
But do it without the song.

29:47.411 --> 29:48.828
Why?

29:48.829 --> 29:51.039
Because I told you,
I don't want to hear it.

29:51.040 --> 29:53.626
- But it's all set to the...
- I'm sure you've got it down.

29:55.503 --> 29:57.378
Why won't you just let me
play it for you?

29:57.379 --> 29:59.006
'Cause I don't want
to break my streak.

29:59.590 --> 30:00.715
Of what?

30:00.716 --> 30:02.218
Of not listening
to your music.

31:44.403 --> 31:45.528
Ooh. Okay.

31:45.529 --> 31:47.114
- Well, I think that's...
- I'm not done yet.

33:26.130 --> 33:29.382
How on earth
are you gonna sing

33:29.383 --> 33:30.968
while you do all that?

33:33.804 --> 33:34.888
Practice.

33:51.405 --> 33:52.531
You know,

33:54.158 --> 33:55.868
if you're going for...

33:56.827 --> 34:01.123
burn-it-all-down
last-will-and-testaments,

34:01.915 --> 34:03.542
what we should do is

34:04.543 --> 34:06.127
we should make you
a beautiful dress

34:06.128 --> 34:07.462
that is simple and elegant,

34:07.463 --> 34:09.005
and whatever else
it needs to be,

34:09.006 --> 34:11.508
but attached to it...

34:12.968 --> 34:14.010
is a train.

34:14.011 --> 34:16.597
You know how I love...

34:18.098 --> 34:20.850
a good train,
and this one is, say,

34:20.851 --> 34:23.311
um, just a quarter-mile long.

34:23.312 --> 34:26.230
And maybe
most people don't notice,

34:26.231 --> 34:29.275
but a keen eye will detect

34:29.276 --> 34:33.447
that at a certain point,
the fabric of the gown fades

34:33.989 --> 34:35.199
from one thing

34:35.824 --> 34:37.617
into something else.

34:37.618 --> 34:40.077
Something more familiar.

34:40.078 --> 34:42.121
It's so seamless
you don't even see it.

34:42.122 --> 34:43.791
But once you do,

34:44.875 --> 34:46.626
you realize

34:46.627 --> 34:51.005
the entire gown is made up
of every dress

34:51.006 --> 34:52.965
you've ever

34:52.966 --> 34:54.675
worn.

34:54.676 --> 34:57.346
The story
of how you got to right here,

34:57.763 --> 34:59.597
right now,

34:59.598 --> 35:02.183
in this exact moment,

35:02.184 --> 35:03.726
stepping out on stage,

35:03.727 --> 35:06.729
Mother Mary...
...in the new millennium.

35:06.730 --> 35:08.564
You walk...

35:08.565 --> 35:09.690
...down the...
Where is the show?

35:09.691 --> 35:13.152
- At the Palladium.
- That's perfect. So...

35:13.153 --> 35:15.863
Miel Contrera
finishes singing,

35:15.864 --> 35:18.783
and it's beautiful
and it's well-liked,

35:18.784 --> 35:22.162
but now, here you come,

35:22.996 --> 35:25.456
marching down that aisle,

35:25.457 --> 35:27.458
marching
from far beyond the aisle,

35:27.459 --> 35:29.168
from outside the theater,

35:29.169 --> 35:30.920
coming down the street,

35:30.921 --> 35:34.925
dragging your whole history
behind you.

35:35.509 --> 35:37.385
The doors swing open,

35:37.386 --> 35:38.553
and you enter the theater

35:38.554 --> 35:41.347
and you walk up
the steps to the stage,

35:41.348 --> 35:43.225
and when you get to the top...

35:43.976 --> 35:45.227
What's this?

35:46.436 --> 35:47.771
Something catches.

35:48.647 --> 35:51.232
The train is pulled tight.

35:51.233 --> 35:55.529
It's caught
on all of your history.

35:56.363 --> 35:59.115
And as you take
your final step

35:59.116 --> 36:01.410
and complete your ascension,

36:02.035 --> 36:04.036
the entire gown,

36:04.037 --> 36:07.498
we'll set it
so it just shears away,

36:07.499 --> 36:08.750
and there you are.

36:09.918 --> 36:15.548
You are standing naked
under the lights,

36:15.549 --> 36:18.217
free of everything
you've been carrying,

36:18.218 --> 36:21.053
of everything that's been
weighing you down.

36:21.054 --> 36:23.180
And, of course,
the plugs will get pulled

36:23.181 --> 36:26.225
and the broadcast would cut
but that's on them,

36:26.226 --> 36:27.727
it's not on you.

36:27.728 --> 36:29.145
Mmm-mmm.

36:29.146 --> 36:31.732
You're doing
what you were born to do.

36:32.608 --> 36:34.942
You open your mouth

36:34.943 --> 36:36.945
and you dance your dance.

36:38.572 --> 36:40.699
You sing your song.

36:41.950 --> 36:43.410
Or maybe...

36:44.620 --> 36:46.121
you don't even do that.

36:47.915 --> 36:49.791
Maybe you don't need to.

36:51.293 --> 36:54.755
You don't need
the song at all,

36:55.464 --> 36:56.965
because this...

36:58.508 --> 37:01.637
is all about...

37:02.971 --> 37:04.056
you.

37:12.564 --> 37:13.649
But...

37:19.488 --> 37:20.948
isn't that kind of...

37:27.746 --> 37:28.872
- obvious?
- No.

37:29.831 --> 37:33.001
Mmm. This is...

37:33.627 --> 37:34.711
clarity.

37:35.712 --> 37:38.840
♪ Bad conversations ♪

37:40.050 --> 37:42.719
♪ Cigarettes ♪

37:43.512 --> 37:46.056
♪ Words I don't mean ♪

37:47.307 --> 37:49.392
♪ Empty threats ♪

37:49.393 --> 37:51.435
♪ Chewing gum ♪

37:51.436 --> 37:54.773
♪ I'm so empty ♪

37:56.400 --> 38:00.112
♪ You're the one for me ♪

38:00.737 --> 38:02.697
♪ You see ♪

38:02.698 --> 38:05.534
♪ But it's been a while ♪

38:09.037 --> 38:13.208
♪ My mouth is lonely for you ♪

38:16.336 --> 38:20.632
♪ My mouth is lonely for you ♪

38:22.676 --> 38:24.553
♪ You ♪

38:26.596 --> 38:28.265
♪ My mouth ♪

38:31.226 --> 38:35.312
♪ My mouth is lonely for you ♪

39:50.263 --> 39:53.140
♪ You said go find
all the things that you want ♪

39:53.141 --> 39:54.809
♪ Find all the things
that you need ♪

39:54.810 --> 39:58.270
♪ If you can't find them in me
go find anywhere, please ♪

39:58.271 --> 40:00.439
♪ Unroll the map
climb up the trees ♪

40:00.440 --> 40:02.358
♪ Scale the mountain
do or don't breathe ♪

40:02.359 --> 40:04.401
♪ But you must
fall to your knees ♪

40:04.402 --> 40:06.862
♪ Don't cry to the stars
you must summon the deep ♪

40:06.863 --> 40:08.489
♪ Lose all the people
you keep ♪

40:08.490 --> 40:09.615
♪ Lose your will to believe ♪

40:09.616 --> 40:10.825
♪ And once again believe ♪

40:10.826 --> 40:12.493
♪ And if in the end
you're not free ♪

40:12.494 --> 40:13.994
♪ Cut a deal, please ♪

40:13.995 --> 40:16.122
♪ Used to walk with you ♪

40:16.123 --> 40:19.708
♪ Till I saw
something bigger ♪

40:19.709 --> 40:21.794
♪ I jumped
into the flames ♪

40:21.795 --> 40:25.172
♪ And I shook hands
with forever ♪

40:25.173 --> 40:28.467
♪ Had to cut ties ♪

40:30.804 --> 40:33.598
♪ To be star-light ♪

40:36.810 --> 40:38.811
♪ He blessed me
with his gaze... ♪

40:38.812 --> 40:42.190
That was a very specific
moment in time,

40:42.774 --> 40:43.942
wasn't it?

40:45.944 --> 40:47.404
Why do we say that?

40:48.488 --> 40:50.531
Every moment in time
is specific.

40:50.532 --> 40:53.702
Yeah, but it's hard to tell
one from the next. Mmm?

40:54.619 --> 40:56.329
Every now and then, though,

40:57.330 --> 40:59.207
something happens.

41:00.375 --> 41:02.543
And it makes us
prick up our ears

41:02.544 --> 41:06.463
and say,
"That was a moment."

41:06.464 --> 41:09.425
And what I think
we're really saying...

41:09.426 --> 41:11.303
...is for that moment,

41:12.888 --> 41:14.848
we were...

41:15.599 --> 41:16.641
together.

41:19.394 --> 41:21.563
Did you really mean
what you said?

41:22.355 --> 41:24.356
About what?

41:24.357 --> 41:26.776
About not listening
to my music.

41:30.155 --> 41:31.489
Yes.

41:32.616 --> 41:33.741
Is it a surprise?

41:33.742 --> 41:35.951
I don't exactly see you
at the runway.

41:35.952 --> 41:38.662
Did I really hurt
your feelings so badly?

41:38.663 --> 41:39.872
Yeah.

41:39.873 --> 41:41.707
And that's fine.

41:41.708 --> 41:43.709
That's what feelings are for.

41:43.710 --> 41:46.004
I just wish you would have
told me yourself.

41:47.172 --> 41:48.380
Told you what?

41:48.381 --> 41:50.258
That, um...

41:51.259 --> 41:53.510
That Mother Mary no longer
needed me.

41:53.511 --> 41:55.638
- I did need you.
- No, you...

41:55.639 --> 41:57.389
- And I did tell you.
- You told me

41:57.390 --> 41:58.682
by not telling me.

41:58.683 --> 42:00.059
You told me by saying nothing

42:00.060 --> 42:02.603
and letting everyone
who suddenly had your ear

42:02.604 --> 42:03.646
do all the talking.

42:03.647 --> 42:04.939
I told you I needed a change.

42:04.940 --> 42:07.942
Yes, but you didn't tell me
you'd already made it.

42:07.943 --> 42:09.735
By the time
I figured that out,

42:09.736 --> 42:11.904
you'd already closed the door.

42:11.905 --> 42:13.197
The door was always open.

42:13.198 --> 42:14.281
No.

42:14.282 --> 42:15.367
No, it wasn't.

42:16.660 --> 42:18.662
No, it wasn't. It was shut

42:19.120 --> 42:20.663
and locked.

42:20.664 --> 42:22.874
And you were
a million miles away.

42:23.750 --> 42:25.334
And there I was...

42:25.335 --> 42:27.045
who knew you and...

42:29.839 --> 42:31.424
who loved you,

42:32.717 --> 42:36.095
trying to pick up the pieces.

42:36.096 --> 42:38.973
Except there weren't
even any pieces

42:38.974 --> 42:40.809
'cause everything I had was...

42:41.601 --> 42:43.852
wrapped up in you.

42:43.853 --> 42:46.313
You never know
how little you matter

42:46.314 --> 42:48.023
until you realize

42:48.024 --> 42:49.817
that everything you've done

42:49.818 --> 42:51.652
has been in the service

42:51.653 --> 42:54.113
of someone
the whole world loves

42:54.114 --> 42:56.366
just as much as you.

42:59.536 --> 43:03.497
Oh, yeah. And tell yourself
you're doing good work.

43:03.498 --> 43:05.082
Tell yourself
what you're doing counts

43:05.083 --> 43:06.542
'cause you're the one
that's doing it,

43:06.543 --> 43:09.586
but really, step by step,

43:09.587 --> 43:10.964
stitch by stitch,

43:12.882 --> 43:15.051
you're obliterating yourself.

43:20.015 --> 43:22.099
I wanted you

43:22.100 --> 43:23.810
to look like Joan of Arc.

43:27.230 --> 43:29.024
When I heard you sing,

43:29.941 --> 43:32.234
that's what I saw.

43:32.235 --> 43:36.573
That's what I set out
to design for you.

43:37.407 --> 43:38.700
And to that,

43:39.326 --> 43:42.120
I added bits and pieces

43:43.705 --> 43:44.706
of me.

43:46.750 --> 43:48.084
Silly things,

43:49.002 --> 43:52.338
like my holy communion
when I was seven.

43:52.339 --> 43:53.380
Feeling like a queen

43:53.381 --> 43:54.923
even though I'd spilled wine

43:54.924 --> 43:57.177
all down
my beautiful white dress.

44:00.221 --> 44:01.306
All of that

44:02.515 --> 44:03.725
is in there.

44:05.643 --> 44:07.228
That's my story.

44:08.855 --> 44:09.898
And no,

44:10.690 --> 44:12.275
I don't expect you to tell it.

44:13.526 --> 44:16.988
But I... would have expected
a little bit credit.

44:26.539 --> 44:29.209
- I didn't mean to cut you out.
- But you did.

44:30.502 --> 44:31.628
Yes.

44:32.379 --> 44:33.380
I did.

44:36.758 --> 44:38.634
- But...
- What?

44:38.635 --> 44:40.887
But I'm the one
who wore that dress,

44:42.597 --> 44:44.557
who wore all the dresses.

44:46.893 --> 44:47.976
I let you make

44:47.977 --> 44:50.354
- something of me.
- No. No.

44:50.355 --> 44:52.773
- We did that together.
- And...

44:52.774 --> 44:53.983
And I liked it.

44:54.943 --> 44:56.069
I liked it.

44:58.029 --> 44:59.739
I liked how you saw me.

45:03.451 --> 45:05.078
I liked how it felt...

45:07.288 --> 45:09.706
when you dressed me.

45:09.707 --> 45:13.085
But you were making
your own Mother Mary,

45:13.086 --> 45:14.337
and she...

45:14.879 --> 45:16.464
she was beautiful.

45:17.674 --> 45:19.216
But I'm the one
who had to go out

45:19.217 --> 45:20.844
in front of all those people

45:21.469 --> 45:23.263
and sing my songs

45:23.930 --> 45:26.181
and feel them, so, yes...

45:27.225 --> 45:29.853
...I wanted to change for her.

45:31.020 --> 45:32.897
But I was never done with us.

45:34.566 --> 45:35.983
You closed that door.

45:35.984 --> 45:38.861
No, there was never a door
at all until you opened it.

45:38.862 --> 45:39.945
The door doesn't exist.

45:39.946 --> 45:41.948
These metaphors
are exhausting.

45:45.243 --> 45:47.619
You went somewhere...

45:47.620 --> 45:50.205
- I couldn't follow.
- Yes, but you had all this.

45:50.206 --> 45:52.166
Yeah, I had to build this
so I had something.

45:52.167 --> 45:53.709
But that's good, isn't it?

45:53.710 --> 45:55.669
Yeah.

45:55.670 --> 45:58.381
Except that it took me
hating you to do it.

46:05.305 --> 46:07.140
Uh-uh.

46:24.240 --> 46:25.782
You can't really hate me.

46:25.783 --> 46:26.868
Oh, yes, I can.

46:27.869 --> 46:30.537
It's very easy
to flip that switch.

46:30.538 --> 46:32.414
Is that what we're doing here?

46:32.415 --> 46:34.333
You're making me a hate-dress?

46:34.334 --> 46:35.710
Maybe.

46:36.503 --> 46:37.753
Maybe.

46:37.754 --> 46:40.047
So what do we have to do
to flip that switch back?

46:40.048 --> 46:42.716
I don't know. Maybe we can't,
maybe it's a one-time thing.

46:42.717 --> 46:43.718
No.

46:44.385 --> 46:45.886
You already have.

46:45.887 --> 46:47.846
You wouldn't let me
in the door otherwise.

46:47.847 --> 46:50.349
The real door
or the metaphorical one?

46:50.350 --> 46:51.850
- Your front door.
- Oh.

46:51.851 --> 46:53.978
Well... I didn't let you in.

46:55.146 --> 46:56.980
Hilda did.

46:56.981 --> 46:59.733
And why do I have to be
the one to open the door

46:59.734 --> 47:01.903
or flip a switch or whatever?

47:03.821 --> 47:05.198
Can't you do it?

47:07.283 --> 47:08.910
Can't you do the work?

47:10.870 --> 47:13.581
Make me love you again.

47:14.582 --> 47:16.292
Can you let me try?

47:17.669 --> 47:19.419
Can you stop putting up walls?

47:19.420 --> 47:22.089
Can you let me play
this fucking song?

47:22.090 --> 47:24.132
Oh, you can't do
anything else?

47:24.133 --> 47:25.969
I don't have anything else.

47:26.928 --> 47:28.303
What else is there?

47:28.304 --> 47:30.722
I can... send you flowers,

47:30.723 --> 47:32.683
I can write you a note,
or I can buy you a house,

47:32.684 --> 47:35.728
or I can sing you a song.
That's it.

47:40.692 --> 47:41.818
That's all I got.

47:45.238 --> 47:47.072
Well, I could do
with a new house.

47:47.073 --> 47:48.783
This one's falling apart.

47:50.618 --> 47:52.411
Pick one out
and send me the listing.

47:52.412 --> 47:54.204
Oh, you know, I think
I'll pay for it myself.

47:54.205 --> 47:56.206
Thank you very much.

47:56.207 --> 47:58.250
You see, the problem is,

47:58.251 --> 48:01.086
and it's not a problem,

48:01.087 --> 48:03.172
but the problem is...

48:04.007 --> 48:06.676
I am very stubborn.

48:09.470 --> 48:10.680
Clearly.

48:11.389 --> 48:13.807
And I don't...

48:13.808 --> 48:17.770
I'm no good
at changing on the spot.

48:18.938 --> 48:20.148
I'm not...

48:20.732 --> 48:22.233
like you.

48:23.484 --> 48:25.944
I can't be what other people
want me to be

48:25.945 --> 48:27.322
at the drop of a hat.

48:27.989 --> 48:29.282
Good.

48:30.074 --> 48:31.700
Because it wears you down.

48:31.701 --> 48:34.703
And I've been getting on
quite well without you.

48:34.704 --> 48:37.039
If I hear you on the radio,
I change the channel.

48:37.040 --> 48:39.459
If I see you on the telly,
I just turn it off.

48:41.044 --> 48:42.587
All or nothing.

48:44.505 --> 48:45.965
All or nothing.

48:48.426 --> 48:50.470
Everyone else needs you.

48:51.846 --> 48:53.389
I don't.

48:58.561 --> 49:00.520
Would you like to know
what happened

49:00.521 --> 49:02.690
the last time
I heard you sing?

49:03.900 --> 49:04.900
Sure.

49:04.901 --> 49:06.735
It's gonna sound
like another metaphor,

49:06.736 --> 49:08.195
even though it's not.

49:08.196 --> 49:09.197
Okay.

49:11.866 --> 49:15.661
Do you remember
when you played in Hyde Park

49:15.662 --> 49:17.747
at the beginning
of your Ecstatic Tour?

49:19.374 --> 49:21.376
- Yeah.
- I was there.

49:22.377 --> 49:23.628
Front row.

49:35.306 --> 49:37.891
I wondered
if you'd spot me,

49:37.892 --> 49:40.228
but... you never did.

49:41.187 --> 49:43.773
Or if you did,
you didn't let on.

49:44.482 --> 49:46.484
And now I'm letting on now

49:47.860 --> 49:49.904
you were amazing.

49:50.988 --> 49:54.075
The whole crowd was crying.

49:54.575 --> 49:56.618
You were crying.

49:56.619 --> 49:58.121
And I was crying,

49:58.871 --> 50:01.790
but for a different reason.

50:01.791 --> 50:04.668
Because I was seeing
something beautiful

50:04.669 --> 50:06.461
that I had once been a part of

50:06.462 --> 50:09.298
and... never would be again.

50:11.050 --> 50:12.760
You were radiant.

50:14.512 --> 50:16.264
I was miserable.

50:18.099 --> 50:19.266
And by and by,

50:19.267 --> 50:24.438
that misery resolved
into a very sharp pain

50:24.439 --> 50:26.441
in my upper mandible.

50:27.692 --> 50:30.819
My jaws were clenched so tight

50:30.820 --> 50:34.656
that my top left wisdom tooth
cracked wide open,

50:34.657 --> 50:37.743
and the pain that it gave me

50:37.744 --> 50:39.370
was pure

50:40.413 --> 50:41.664
and sharp.

50:43.166 --> 50:48.503
And I could think of no way
to describe it other than you.

50:54.719 --> 50:56.053
Oh, it was you.

50:56.929 --> 50:59.140
And I had to cut you out.

51:02.769 --> 51:04.270
So I fled.

51:06.606 --> 51:08.857
Before the encore.

51:08.858 --> 51:10.233
Before you played Holy Spirit,

51:10.234 --> 51:12.904
the one song I thought
might make me feel better.

51:15.072 --> 51:16.407
Mary! Mary!

51:18.117 --> 51:19.410
I ran home,

51:20.244 --> 51:21.621
grabbed some pliers,

51:23.748 --> 51:24.916
and...

51:35.259 --> 51:36.385
See?

51:39.680 --> 51:40.932
All gone.

51:42.767 --> 51:43.767
Jesus!

51:43.768 --> 51:45.978
I'm only exaggerating.

51:47.063 --> 51:48.815
I went to the dentist.

51:49.816 --> 51:51.234
Yeah, they put me under,

51:52.485 --> 51:54.987
and when I woke up
in the chair,

51:55.571 --> 51:57.156
my tooth was gone.

51:59.325 --> 52:01.953
And the anesthesia
was wearing off,

52:03.704 --> 52:05.373
and I felt very sad.

52:06.916 --> 52:08.708
Like I was...

52:08.709 --> 52:12.255
in the midst of saying goodbye
to something dear.

52:12.964 --> 52:15.841
You know, when I was little,

52:15.842 --> 52:18.260
and we'd move,

52:18.261 --> 52:23.307
and I'd feel myself
being pulled away from a house

52:23.891 --> 52:26.519
I'd made time to love.

52:30.690 --> 52:31.691
Hmm.

52:34.277 --> 52:35.278
Now...

52:37.488 --> 52:38.990
this is where it gets

52:39.532 --> 52:40.533
strange.

52:41.909 --> 52:43.202
That night,

52:45.329 --> 52:46.581
I had a visitor.

52:48.207 --> 52:49.583
I woke up very suddenly

52:49.584 --> 52:51.669
to find that my gums
were bleeding again.

52:53.838 --> 52:56.381
There was blood all over.

52:56.382 --> 52:59.718
There was a little trail
of it, in fact,

52:59.719 --> 53:02.137
streaked across the duvet.

53:02.138 --> 53:05.349
It was like something had
crawled out of my mouth,

53:06.058 --> 53:07.768
across the bedspread,

53:08.686 --> 53:09.979
down onto the floor.

53:11.230 --> 53:12.356
Now...

53:13.190 --> 53:15.233
I've always been
open to ghosts.

53:15.234 --> 53:17.694
If any house was haunted,
you'd think it'd be this one,

53:17.695 --> 53:20.031
but I haven't seen one before.

53:20.907 --> 53:22.158
Until now.

53:22.909 --> 53:24.826
And I can say
without a doubt,

53:24.827 --> 53:27.830
there was a ghost
at the foot of my bed.

53:31.542 --> 53:33.044
What did it look like?

53:33.753 --> 53:35.879
I couldn't say.

53:35.880 --> 53:39.216
She was like
six different things at once.

53:39.592 --> 53:40.800
"She"?

53:40.801 --> 53:43.220
Yes. She was a she.

53:44.639 --> 53:46.431
I think.

53:46.432 --> 53:50.060
Or maybe the idea of a "she."

53:51.604 --> 53:52.730
And she was red.

53:54.065 --> 53:56.067
Not red like a color.

53:56.734 --> 53:57.985
More like...

53:59.153 --> 54:01.029
red like a feeling.

54:09.705 --> 54:14.919
Oh, and she was
the most beautiful thing.

54:16.003 --> 54:18.172
I couldn't let her stay.

54:21.425 --> 54:23.636
So I opened the door,

54:24.887 --> 54:26.847
and I watched her go,

54:29.100 --> 54:30.518
down the hallway,

54:32.061 --> 54:33.854
out the house,

54:35.064 --> 54:37.482
into the woods,

54:37.483 --> 54:40.069
a smudge of red in the dark.

54:42.863 --> 54:46.617
Oh, and with her goes
the pain in my mouth,

54:48.536 --> 54:50.621
the knot in my stomach,

54:52.164 --> 54:54.625
and the hole in my heart.

54:58.295 --> 55:02.091
And after that I stopped
listening to your music.

55:04.051 --> 55:06.053
I stopped thinking about you.

55:07.179 --> 55:08.931
I stopped dreaming about you.

55:10.516 --> 55:14.270
And everything's been better
ever since.

55:17.481 --> 55:18.691
Where did she go?

55:19.859 --> 55:20.943
Oh.

55:22.069 --> 55:23.738
Oh, I don't know.

55:24.447 --> 55:25.613
Where do ghosts go

55:25.614 --> 55:27.324
when you don't
need 'em anymore?

55:28.159 --> 55:29.451
That's where.

55:29.452 --> 55:32.537
But are you saying that
this is just another metaphor?

55:32.538 --> 55:34.539
Did you really see something?

55:34.540 --> 55:37.417
Look, I'm not saying
that I saw the spirit

55:37.418 --> 55:39.627
of some
recently deceased individual

55:39.628 --> 55:44.049
or that my house
is haunted by an ancestor.

55:44.050 --> 55:45.341
If someone else...

55:45.342 --> 55:49.137
If Hilda, say, had been there,
would she have seen it?

55:49.138 --> 55:50.431
Probably not.

55:51.640 --> 55:52.808
But I did.

55:54.185 --> 55:56.436
Whatever neurons
in my head differentiate

55:56.437 --> 55:58.313
between imagination
and perception

55:58.314 --> 56:00.066
tell me that I did.

56:00.941 --> 56:04.111
And if you were
to ask me why I did,

56:05.071 --> 56:08.574
I would say
because I needed to.

56:09.450 --> 56:11.409
Perhaps I manifested her.

56:11.410 --> 56:15.121
Perhaps she was
my subconscious,

56:15.122 --> 56:16.164
sending me a message

56:16.165 --> 56:18.375
in the only way
it knew I would listen.

56:20.461 --> 56:22.379
Perhaps she was a ghost.

56:23.214 --> 56:24.256
Yeah.

56:27.510 --> 56:29.804
But she was my ghost.

56:31.597 --> 56:32.890
Except...

56:33.724 --> 56:35.601
I think I saw her too.

56:37.186 --> 56:38.603
You saw what?

56:38.604 --> 56:39.813
Your ghost.

56:41.398 --> 56:43.441
- I saw her.
- I was being serious.

56:43.442 --> 56:44.818
So am I.

56:44.819 --> 56:47.112
So what?

56:47.113 --> 56:50.240
You can't even let me
have my own ghost story?

56:50.241 --> 56:52.200
No. No, it is yours.

56:52.201 --> 56:55.286
It is, but I think
I might be a part of it.

56:55.287 --> 56:57.497
You're making me feel

56:57.498 --> 56:59.874
- very foolish.
- I promise I don't mean to.

56:59.875 --> 57:02.168
I saw what you saw.

57:02.169 --> 57:07.925
I saw a ghost or a spirit
and she was red.

57:08.467 --> 57:10.593
And when was this?

57:10.594 --> 57:12.930
- The first time was...
- Ooh. "The first time"?

57:15.349 --> 57:17.226
The first time was in Dublin.

57:19.061 --> 57:20.688
96th stop of the tour.

57:21.480 --> 57:23.691
I was so worn out, but...

57:26.902 --> 57:28.487
it was my birthday.

57:31.073 --> 57:33.534
And I wanted to do
something special.

57:40.666 --> 57:42.750
I love you, Dublin!

57:42.751 --> 57:43.960
Goodnight!

58:09.028 --> 58:11.237
- Thank you.
-Here, here, here.

58:11.238 --> 58:12.780
I've got it. I've got it.
I've got it.

58:12.781 --> 58:14.073
Careful.

58:16.452 --> 58:18.120
How does this keep happening?

58:19.580 --> 58:20.747
Oh, shit. Um,

58:20.748 --> 58:22.290
- there's blood on your...
- Huh?

58:22.291 --> 58:23.291
-Hey, MM!
- Blood...

58:23.292 --> 58:26.211
- Oh, um, yeah.
-Look who I found!

58:26.212 --> 58:27.254
Ooh.

58:27.796 --> 58:29.631
Oh, my gosh!

58:29.632 --> 58:30.798
- Are you...
- Hi.

58:30.799 --> 58:33.843
-  Hi! Hi, hi, hi!
- I'm Imogen. Hi.

58:33.844 --> 58:35.595
Happy birthday.

58:35.596 --> 58:37.305
Thank you. Thank you. Yes.

58:37.306 --> 58:38.890
- So nice to meet you.
- So nice to meet you.

58:38.891 --> 58:41.476
Yes. Oh, my gosh.
We are so excited for tonight.

58:41.477 --> 58:42.727
- Me too.
- Everyone says

58:42.728 --> 58:44.145
you are very special.

58:44.146 --> 58:46.064
- Well, that sounds very kind.
- Okay.

58:46.065 --> 58:47.482
She was sat
in the regular seat,

58:47.483 --> 58:48.733
that's why PJ couldn't
find her.

58:48.734 --> 58:49.984
- Ah.
-How long did you say

58:49.985 --> 58:51.527
- you waited in line?
-Oh?

58:51.528 --> 58:54.322
Only two hours.
But it's fine. I had fun.

58:54.323 --> 58:56.449
- I met people.
- I'm so sorry.

58:56.450 --> 58:57.909
Yeah. Okay.

58:57.910 --> 58:59.994
- I like meeting people.
- Thank you.

58:59.995 --> 59:02.455
Oh, well, now you're here
and you're with us.

59:02.456 --> 59:04.165
Did you like the show?

59:04.166 --> 59:05.959
- Oh, it was incredible.
-Mmm.

59:05.960 --> 59:08.378
It was like,
like a religious experience

59:08.379 --> 59:10.421
or like going to church,

59:10.422 --> 59:13.132
- but in a good way.
-  Yeah.

59:13.133 --> 59:16.052
And at the same time,
all I could think is

59:16.053 --> 59:18.221
when you have
that many people...

59:18.222 --> 59:20.181
- Yeah.
- How many people were there?

59:20.182 --> 59:23.184
Uh, 18,210.

59:23.185 --> 59:25.311
There were even more
in New York.

59:25.312 --> 59:27.689
And they're all there,

59:27.690 --> 59:31.109
all at once,
putting out all that energy,

59:31.110 --> 59:33.069
all of those ups and downs,

59:33.070 --> 59:39.784
and all of it is
laser-focused right at you.

59:39.785 --> 59:42.245
Mmm. It's intense.

59:42.246 --> 59:43.622
How do you handle that?

59:44.498 --> 59:46.457
You don't.

59:46.458 --> 59:48.501
Uh, I mean, you do.

59:48.502 --> 59:49.711
But you just...

59:49.712 --> 59:50.963
You sort of, um,

59:51.630 --> 59:52.631
take it

59:53.299 --> 59:54.383
and...

01:00:00.931 --> 01:00:02.391
Yes, but...

01:00:03.642 --> 01:00:05.561
what does it do to you?

01:00:08.856 --> 01:00:10.940
It's like the same, same thing

01:00:10.941 --> 01:00:14.027
over and over again
in circles.

01:00:14.028 --> 01:00:15.236
Sounds like shit.

01:00:15.237 --> 01:00:17.280
Don't ask
why he chose me, but he did.

01:00:17.281 --> 01:00:19.949
But you have seen
ghosts here before, right?

01:00:19.950 --> 01:00:21.367
Ah, yes.

01:00:21.368 --> 01:00:23.077
There are spirits here

01:00:23.078 --> 01:00:24.871
and I've met most of them.

01:00:24.872 --> 01:00:27.582
But the walls here
are very thin.

01:00:27.583 --> 01:00:29.917
You never know
who might come knocking.

01:00:29.918 --> 01:00:32.962
Now, can somebody
get the lights?

01:00:32.963 --> 01:00:34.255
Do ghosts really need the dark

01:00:34.256 --> 01:00:36.591
or is it just
to make it spookier?

01:00:36.592 --> 01:00:38.384
Oh, it's not for them.

